SEC. 40001. COAST GUARD MISSION READINESS.

This section appropriates $24,593,500,000 to the Coast Guard for fiscal year 2025, available until September 30, 2029, for new assets, maintenance, shore infrastructure, and operational resilience. The funds are allocated across specific procurement categories, including $1,142,500,000 for fixed-wing aircraft, $2,283,000,000 for rotary-wing aircraft, $266,000,000 for long-range unmanned aircraft, $4,300,000,000 for Offshore Patrol Cutters, $1,000,000,000 for Fast Response Cutters, $4,300,000,000 for Polar Security Cutters, $3,500,000,000 for Arctic Security Cutters, $816,000,000 for light and medium icebreakers, and $162,000,000 for Waterways Commerce Cutters. It also provides $4,379,000,000 for shore facility improvements, including specific allocations for boot camp barracks, the Coast Guard Yard, and homeports. Additional funds cover depot maintenance ($2,200,000,000), maritime domain awareness ($170,000,000), and autonomous maritime systems ($75,000,000). [end of text]


